{
  "title": "DNA",
  "summary": "DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid) is the hereditary material in almost all living organisms. It contains the genetic instructions used in the growth, development, functioning, and reproduction of all known life forms. DNA molecules consist of two strands forming a double helix, composed of nucleotides with bases adenine, thymine, cytosine, and guanine. The sequence of these bases encodes genetic information."
}
